      "id": 1,
      "text": "After a 1953 flood triggered by Falcon Dam, New Falcon was moved from its original site to preserve the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.texasalmanac.com/places/falcon-0",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was renamed Falcon to honor Margarita de la Garza Falcón, the wife of founder José Clemente Ramírez.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.texasalmanac.com/places/falcon-0",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Originally called Ramireño de Abajo, the area was part of a 6,123‑acre grant to José Clemente Gutiérrez in the 1700s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.texasalmanac.com/places/falcon-0",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
